# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored; this file is not, so never put
# a real value here.
#
# Run with:  uv run --env-file .env uvicorn server:app --port 8080
# On Railway these are the service's Variables; there is no file.
#
# Both are required, and they are all there is. The service holds no Día
# login and no card: every job brings the shopper's login (their encrypted
# profile in the web app) and the card to pay with (the web app's
# `shared_card` row). For a CLI run, put both in a --job JSON file instead.

# ---- the job API -----------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token the web app sends on /jobs. Any long random string:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Must equal SANDBOX_TOKEN in the web app (Vercel). The two services share
# this one value and nothing else.
SANDBOX_TOKEN=

# ---- Jev -------------------------------------------------------------------
# TypeSafe API key. Jev (System One) picks the next action at every step; it
# never sees a login or a card, only "type the password into its field".
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# ---- optional --------------------------------------------------------------
# Railway sets PORT itself; the Dockerfile defaults to 8080. Leave it unset.
# PORT=8080
